# =============================================================================
# SECRETS AND SIGNING MATERIAL
#
# This repository is public. A published signing keystore cannot be revoked —
# only rotated, which for Play Store means an upload-key reset — and a published
# API key has to be assumed compromised the moment it lands. Nothing in this
# section may ever be committed, including "just for a moment".
# =============================================================================
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
key.properties
key.properties.txt
**/key.properties
**/key.properties.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
service-account*.json
secrets.json

# Firebase config. It ships inside the APK, so it is not a secret in the strict
# sense — but in a public repo it hands over project identifiers for free, and
# nothing here needs it to build.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# =============================================================================
# ANOTHER PROJECT'S SOURCE CODE
#
# The Probahini chatbot from the Ananya app was copied into this folder as a
# reference implementation while Bharosha was being built. It is not WaterAid's
# code to publish, and Probahini.ipynb contains a live-looking Groq API key in
# plain text in cell 10. Bharosha does not import any of it.
# =============================================================================
/stop_gender_violence_fresh_ui/Probahini.ipynb
/stop_gender_violence_fresh_ui/app/
/stop_gender_violence_fresh_ui/Dockerfile.api

